flowchart LR
    Socket["<b>1. socket()</b><br/>allocates struct socket plus TCP struct sock<br/><b>handoff:</b> app chooses passive listen or active connect<br/><b>state:</b> initialized, unbound TCP socket"]

    Passive["<b>2a. passive open</b><br/>bind reserves local port, listen inserts listener, SYN creates request_sock<br/><b>handoff:</b> completed handshake moves child to accept queue<br/><b>state:</b> listener and half-open requests are indexed"]

    Active["<b>2b. active open</b><br/>connect selects source port, routes, sends SYN<br/><b>handoff:</b> SYN-ACK completes the 4-tuple<br/><b>state:</b> client socket moves through SYN_SENT to established hash"]

    Established["<b>3. established stream</b><br/>4-tuple lookup finds the owner socket on RX<br/><b>handoff:</b> application I/O can use TCP queues<br/><b>state:</b> full-duplex stream with cwnd/rwnd state"]

    IO["<b>4. sendmsg / recvmsg</b><br/>move bytes between user buffers and TCP queues<br/><b>handoff:</b> more I/O or close depends on stream state<br/><b>state:</b> write queue, receive queue, timers, and ACK state evolve"]

    Close["<b>5. close</b><br/>drives FIN/RST/TIME_WAIT and unhashes when safe<br/><b>state:</b> fd is gone, protocol state may outlive it"]

    Socket --> Passive --> Established --> IO --> Close
    Socket --> Active --> Established

